  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Somen Dey vs The State Of West Bengal & Ors on 1 July, 2025 01-07-2025 Item No.615 Ml In The High Court At Calcutta Subrata Constitutional Writ Jurisdiction Bhattacharyya Appellate Side Ar(C) Wpa No.19869 of 2024 Somen Dey -vs- The State of West Bengal & Ors. Ms. Rinku Sen Mr. Sagnik Bhattacharya Ms. Raksar Parveen ...for the petitioner Mr. Asish Kumar Guha Mr. Jayak Kumar Gupta ...for the State Mr. Amit Meharia Mr. Tannishta Singh Ms. Parmita Banerjee Mr. Sayan Dey ...for respondents no.4, 5 & 7 Ms. Tanushree Dasgupta ...for the Corporation 1. The petitioner alleges illegal running of business by the private respondent without obtaining proper permission/licence from the fire and emergency services and the pollution control board.",
    "facts": "1. The petitioner alleges illegal running of business by the private respondent without obtaining proper permission/licence from the fire and emergency services and the pollution control board. 2. The petitioner submits that the private respondent is manufacturing food items from the subject premises which are causing threat to his health. 3. None represents the pollution control board. 4. Learned counsel for the Kolkata Municipal Corporation relies upon the instruction forwarded by the Food Safety Officer of the Kolkata Municipal Corporation, Borough-VIII dated July 30, 2024 wherefrom it appears that the subject unit was found non-functional on the day of the inspection on July 10, 2024. 5. The private respondent was present at the premises but could not submit any FSSAI registration certificate/licence in support of the business. A refrain notice was issued to the private respondent on July 10, 2024. Further inspections were carried out on July 15, 2024 and July 19, 2024 when the business was found to be non-functional. 6. As it appears that the Corporation has already taken steps in the matter and issued a refrain notice to the private respondent, let the private respondent not operate the business till proper Somen Dey vs The State Of West Bengal & Ors on 1 July, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/5016193/ 1 7. The Officer-in-Charge of Rabindra Sarabor police station is directed to keep strict vigil in the subject area so that the private respondent does not in any way commence the business contrary to the provisions of law.",
